## [Creating an editing component](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Frameworks_libraries/Vue_conditional_rendering#creating_an_editing_component)
We can start by creating a separate component to handle the editing functionality. In your `components` directory, create a new file called `ToDoItemEditForm.vue`. Copy the following code into that file:
vueCopy to Clipboard
```
<template>
  <form class="stack-small" @submit.prevent="onSubmit">
    <div>
      <label class="edit-label">Edit Name for &quot;{{ label }}&quot;</label>
      <input
        :id="id"
        type="text"
        autocomplete="off"
        v-model.lazy.trim="newLabel" />
    </div>
    <div class="btn-group">
      <button type="button" class="btn" @click="onCancel">
        Cancel
        <span class="visually-hidden">editing {{ label }}</span>
      </button>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn__primary">
        Save
        <span class="visually-hidden">edit for {{ label }}</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </form>
</template>
<script>
export default {
  props: {
    label: {
      type: String,
      required: true,
    },
    id: {
      type: String,
      required: true,
    },
  },
  data() {
    return {
      newLabel: this.label,
    };
  },
  methods: {
    onSubmit() {
      if (this.newLabel && this.newLabel !== this.label) {
        this.$emit("item-edited", this.newLabel);
      }
    },
    onCancel() {
      this.$emit("edit-cancelled");
    },
  },
};
</script>
<style scoped>
