Finally, we've also got an [onchange](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/HTMLElement/change_event) event listener that serves to run a function containing a ternary operator. It starts with a test condition — `select.value === 'black'`. If this returns `true`, we run the `update()` function with parameters of black and white, meaning that we end up with a background color of black and a text color of white. If it returns `false`, we run the `update()` function with parameters of white and black, meaning that the site colors are inverted.
