In this lesson we'll look at arrays — a neat way of storing a list of data items under a single variable name. Here we look at why this is useful, then explore how to create an [array](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array), retrieve, add, and remove items stored in an array, and more besides.
Prerequisites: | An understanding of [HTML](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Structuring_content) and the [fundamentals of CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Learn_web_development/Core/Styling_basics). familiarity with basic data types such as numbers and strings, as covered in previous lessons.  
---|---  
Learning outcomes: | 
