The first block that uses Fetch can be found at the start of the JavaScript:
jsCopy to Clipboard
```
fetch("products.json")
  .then((response) => {
    if (!response.ok) {
      throw new Error(`HTTP error: ${response.status}`);
    }
    return response.json();
  })
  .then((json) => initialize(json))
