  2. Add some useful functions to this `<script>` element below the two existing lines:
jsCopy to Clipboard
```
function squared(num) {
  return num * num;
}

function cubed(num) {
  return num * num * num;
}

function factorial(num) {
  if (num < 0) return undefined;
  if (num === 0) return 1;
  let x = num - 1;
  while (x > 1) {
    num *= x;
    x--;
  }
  return num;
}

```

The `squared()` and `cubed()` functions are fairly obvious — they return the square or cube of the number that was given as a parameter. The `factorial()` function returns the 
