The **`AudioWorkletGlobalScope`**interface of the[Web Audio API](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Web_Audio_API) represents a global execution context for user-supplied code, which defines custom [`AudioWorkletProcessor`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AudioWorkletProcessor)-derived classes.
Each [`BaseAudioContext`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/BaseAudioContext) has a single [`AudioWorklet`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AudioWorklet) available under the [`audioWorklet`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/BaseAudioContext/audioWorklet "audioWorklet") property, which runs its code in a single `AudioWorkletGlobalScope`.
As the global execution context is shared across the current `BaseAudioContext`, it's possible to define any other variables and perform any actions allowed in worklets — apart from defining `AudioWorkletProcessor` derived classes.
