The **`CSSKeyframesRule`**interface describes an object representing a complete set of keyframes for a CSS animation. It corresponds to the contents of a whole[`@keyframes`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@keyframes) [at-rule](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/CSS_syntax/At-rule).
[ CSSRule  ](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSRule)[ CSSKeyframesRule  ](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule)
## [Instance properties](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule#instance_properties)
_Inherits properties from its ancestor[`CSSRule`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSRule)._ 

[`CSSKeyframesRule.name`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule/name)

Represents the name of the keyframes, used by the [`animation-name`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/animation-name) property. 

[`CSSKeyframesRule.cssRules`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule/cssRules) Read only 

Returns a [`CSSRuleList`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSRuleList) of the keyframes in the list. 

[`CSSKeyframesRule.length`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule/length) Read only 

Returns the number of keyframes in the list.
## [Instance methods](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule#instance_methods)
_Inherits methods from its ancestor[`CSSRule`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSRule)._ 

[`CSSKeyframesRule.appendRule()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule/appendRule)

Inserts a new keyframe rule into the current CSSKeyframesRule. The parameter is a string containing a keyframe in the same format as an entry of a [`@keyframes`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/@keyframes) at-rule. If it contains more than one keyframe rule, a [`DOMException`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/DOMException) with a `SYNTAX_ERR` is thrown. 

[`CSSKeyframesRule.deleteRule()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule/deleteRule)

Deletes a keyframe rule from the current CSSKeyframesRule. The parameter is the index of the keyframe to be deleted, expressed as a string resolving as a number between `0%` and `100%`. 

[`CSSKeyframesRule.findRule()`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule/findRule)

Returns a keyframe rule corresponding to the given key. The key is a string containing an index of the keyframe to be returned, resolving to a percentage between `0%` and `100%`. If no such keyframe exists, `findRule` returns `null`.
## [Example](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule#example)
### [Using CSSKeyframesRule](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule#using_csskeyframesrule)
The CSS includes a keyframes at-rule. This will be the first [`CSSRule`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSRule) returned by `document.styleSheets[0].cssRules`. `myRules[0]` returns a `CSSKeyframesRule` object.
cssCopy to Clipboard
```
@keyframes slide-in {
  from {
    transform: translateX(0%);
  }

  to {
    transform: translateX(100%);
  }
}

```

jsCopy to Clipboard
```
const myRules = document.styleSheets[0].cssRules;
const keyframes = myRules[0]; // a CSSKeyframesRule

```

### [Accessing indexes](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule#accessing_indexes)
`CSSKeyframesRule` can be indexed like an array, and functions similar to its [`cssRules`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSSKeyframesRule/cssRules "cssRules") property.
jsCopy to Clipboard
```
const keyframes = document.styleSheets[0].cssRules[0];

for (let i = 0; i < keyframes.length; i++) {
  console.log(keyframes[i].keyText);
}

// Output:
// 0%
// 100%

```

